Node.js (https://github.com/nodejs/node) is licensed under the MIT License,
Copyright Node.js contributors. The iPhoneOS runtime shipped in the `.deb` is
built from the MIT-licensed nodejs-mobile patch set
(https://github.com/nodejs-mobile/nodejs-mobile, Copyright nodejs-mobile
contributors), which is itself derived from Node.js. Both are MIT-licensed; see
`NOTICE` for the full attribution and for the third-party components bundled
inside the Node.js binary (V8, OpenSSL, ICU, libuv, zlib, ...), which carry their
own licenses.

The exact pins, commits and upstream URLs are recorded in `UPSTREAM.lock`, and
the packaged copy of this attribution is installed at
`/var/jb/usr/share/doc/opencode/copyright` by `OpenCode-iOS-rootless.deb`.
